Naming and packaging

  * Package name: v7unix-toolchain.

  * User-facing binaries are prefixed `v7` and installed in the bin dir:
        cc -> v7cc    as -> v7as    ld -> v7ld    make -> v7make    yacc -> v7yacc

  * Internal binaries keep their original names (c0, c1, c2, as2, cpp), and
    libraries keep theirs (crt0.o, ...).  They live under a `v7unix` directory
    (not `v7unix-toolchain`), at the OS's standard filesystem locations:
        /usr/libexec/v7unix/   internal executables (c0, c1, c2, as2, cpp, ...)
        /usr/lib/v7unix/       libraries (crt0.o, libc.a, ...)
        /usr/include/v7unix/   include files

  * Package for the top 20 Linux and BSD distros with full GNU autotools
    packaging (configure.ac, Makefile.in, install/uninstall/check/dist).
